winebus: SDL leaves a pad the hidraw route owns alone.

A DualSense whose key says Hidraw is served by bus_iohid.c, and main.c ignores
the copy of it that the SDL bus reports. Ignoring that copy was never the same
as SDL leaving the pad alone, and on this engine it is not.

WHAT WAS MEASURED, in one bottle, with the pad on Bluetooth and mgvf-0006's
seize on:

- sdl_add_device 054c/0df2 is traced 4 ms before bus_iohid.c's seize
  (hid-203611.log, 333081.353 against 333081.357);
- ioreg shows a second IOHIDLibUserClient on the pad from the same
  winedevice.exe, the process that loads winebus.so and
  lib64/libSDL2-2.0.0.dylib. It has ClientOptions 0, is locked out by the
  seize, and its SetReportErrCnt climbs at exactly 2.00/s (3251 to 4050 over
  399.7 s);
- that libSDL2 has a single IOHIDDeviceOpen call, with options 0.

What ties that client to SDL is read, not traced. sdl_device_stop closes only
the joystick, so SDL's hidapi handle outlives the SDL device main.c threw away.
And SDL 2.30's PS5 driver, when nothing else is written, sends a Bluetooth
keep-alive every 500 ms -- a 78-byte 0x31 with no CRC -- which is the rate.
Under the seize every one of those writes is refused. Without the seize
(SeizeDevice 0, or any moment it is not held) it would be a third writer on a
pad whose link already drops under contention.

THE CHANGE. Before SDL_Init, the SDL bus lists the pads the hidraw route owns
and gives the list to SDL twice:

- SDL_HIDAPI_IGNORE_DEVICES, which SDL's hid enumeration reads on every pass
  (src/hidapi/mac/hid.c), so hidapi never lists the pad and no driver opens
  it;
- SDL_GAMECONTROLLER_IGNORE_DEVICES, which SDL_JoystickInit loads before any
  joystick backend starts. The first list alone is not enough: hidapi letting
  go of a pad is exactly what makes the IOKit backend (HIDAPI_IsDevicePresent)
  and the GameController backend (HIDAPI_IsDeviceTypePresent) take it, and
  both check this list before they add a device.

Both hint names, and both of hidapi's match formats ("0x%.4x/0x%.4x" and
"0x%.4x/0x0000"), are in the engine's libSDL2, 2.30.12 by its dylib version.
SDL lets the environment win over SDL_SetHint, so a user who sets either
variable keeps it, and a WARN says so.

THE SCOPE is what is_hidraw_enabled decides from a device key: a key under
winebus\Devices naming a vendor AND a product, with a non-zero Hidraw, and no
DisableHidraw. The launcher writes Hidraw 1 for its raw route and 0 for its SDL
route, so the SDL route is untouched. Also left exactly as before:

- a pad with no Hidraw value, even one that is_hidraw_enabled sends raw by its
  own preference for Sony pads -- that is a default, not a key saying so;
- a key naming only a vendor, which SDL's second list cannot express;
- product 0000, which SDL's hidapi reads as every product of the vendor.

main.c ignored these pads' SDL devices before this patch and still does, so
nothing a game enumerates changes.

WHAT THIS IS NOT.

- It does not make the second client leave ioreg. Measured on 2026-09-14 with
  the patch (hid-090147.log has the trace line below): the winedevice.exe
  client with ClientOptions 0 showed SetReportErrCnt 0 and SetReportCnt 0
  across a 20 s sample, where before it climbed at 2.00/s. One shared client
  with every counter at zero remains; that it is the IOKit backend's HID
  manager is a reading.
- SDL's IOKit backend opens its HID manager with options 0 at SDL_Init, before
  any list is consulted. That is read from source, is not changed here, and
  only reads.
- The GameController backend names every DualSense 054c:0ce6, so a key for
  the Edge alone does not keep that one backend away from it. Whether that
  backend sees a pad at all inside winedevice.exe is not measured.
- macOS's idle disconnect is a different mechanism, and this does not affect
  it.

Trace (+hid): "SDL will not open 0x054c/0x0ce6,0x054c/0x0df2: the hidraw
route owns them".

Signed-off-by: MacGameVideoFix
---
--- a/dlls/winebus.sys/bus_sdl.c
+++ b/dlls/winebus.sys/bus_sdl.c
@@ -1073,6 +1073,72 @@
     pthread_mutex_unlock(&sdl_cs);
 }
 
+/* MGVF mgvf-0032: SDL leaves a pad the hidraw route owns alone.
+ *
+ * THE PROBLEM. This bus starts SDL over every game controller, and SDL's
+ * hidapi opens a DualSense for its PS5 driver -- in the traces 4 ms before
+ * bus_iohid.c seizes it. main.c then ignores the SDL device, because the pad's
+ * key says Hidraw, but sdl_device_stop closes only the joystick, so SDL's own
+ * handle on the pad stays open for the life of the bottle. ioreg shows that
+ * handle as a second winedevice.exe client, ClientOptions 0, whose
+ * SetReportErrCnt climbs at 2.00/s against mgvf-0006's seize. SDL 2.30's PS5
+ * driver sends a Bluetooth keep-alive, a 78-byte 0x31 with no CRC, every
+ * 500 ms; the rate and the source are what tie the two, no trace of SDL's own
+ * writes does. Without the seize it would be a third writer on the pad.
+ *
+ * THE CHANGE. Before SDL_Init, name those pads in two of SDL's own hints.
+ * SDL_HIDAPI_IGNORE_DEVICES is read on every hid enumeration, so hidapi never
+ * lists them and nothing opens them for a driver. SDL_GAMECONTROLLER_IGNORE_DEVICES
+ * is loaded in SDL_JoystickInit before any joystick backend starts, and the
+ * IOKit and GameController backends -- which would otherwise take a pad the
+ * moment hidapi stops claiming it -- both check it before they add a device.
+ * main.c never kept these pads from SDL in any case, so no game sees a
+ * difference.
+ *
+ * THE SCOPE. What is_hidraw_enabled decides from a device key, and nothing
+ * wider: a key naming a vendor AND a product, with a non-zero Hidraw. A pad
+ * with no Hidraw value, a Hidraw of 0, a key naming only a vendor, and every
+ * pad under DisableHidraw reach SDL exactly as before. Product 0000 is left
+ * out too, because SDL's hidapi reads 0x0000 as every product of the vendor.
+ * The GameController backend names every DualSense 054c:0ce6, so a key for
+ * the Edge alone does not reach that one backend.
+ */
+static void sdl_leave_hidraw_devices_alone(void)
+{
+    const struct device_options *device;
+    SDL_bool hidapi, controller;
+    char list[512];
+    size_t len = 0;
+    int ret;
+
+    if (options->disable_hidraw) return;
+
+    LIST_FOR_EACH_ENTRY(device, &options->devices, struct device_options, entry)
+    {
+        if (device->pid == -1 || !device->pid || device->vid > 0xffff || device->pid > 0xffff) continue;
+        if (device->hidraw == -1 || !device->hidraw) continue;
+
+        ret = snprintf(list + len, sizeof(list) - len, "%s0x%04x/0x%04x", len ? "," : "", device->vid, device->pid);
+        if (ret < 0 || (size_t)ret >= sizeof(list) - len)
+        {
+            list[len] = 0;
+            WARN("too many hidraw devices for SDL's ignore lists, stopping after %s\n", debugstr_a(list));
+            break;
+        }
+        len += ret;
+    }
+    if (!len) return;
+
+    hidapi = pSDL_SetHint(SDL_HINT_HIDAPI_IGNORE_DEVICES, list);
+    controller = pSDL_SetHint(SDL_HINT_GAMECONTROLLER_IGNORE_DEVICES, list);
+    if (hidapi && controller)
+        TRACE("SDL will not open %s: the hidraw route owns them\n", list);
+    else
+        WARN("SDL may still open %s, which the hidraw route owns: %s set in the environment, and SDL lets the environment win\n",
+             list, !hidapi && !controller ? SDL_HINT_HIDAPI_IGNORE_DEVICES " and " SDL_HINT_GAMECONTROLLER_IGNORE_DEVICES " are" :
+             !hidapi ? SDL_HINT_HIDAPI_IGNORE_DEVICES " is" : SDL_HINT_GAMECONTROLLER_IGNORE_DEVICES " is");
+}
+
 NTSTATUS sdl_bus_init(void *args)
 {
     const char *mapping;
@@ -1156,6 +1222,9 @@
     pSDL_SetHint(SDL_HINT_JOYSTICK_HIDAPI_PS5_RUMBLE, "1");
 #endif
 
+    /* MGVF mgvf-0032: before SDL_Init, which is when SDL first enumerates */
+    sdl_leave_hidraw_devices_alone();
+
     if (pSDL_Init(SDL_INIT_GAMECONTROLLER | SDL_INIT_HAPTIC) < 0)
     {
         ERR("could not init SDL: %s\n", pSDL_GetError());
